[34mCommentBareTodo[m
A TODO names an issue or a URL.
Why: A TODO on its own reads like a plan and goes stale in place.
A reference says where the work is tracked, and a made-up one points nowhere.
Instead: If the work is small and part of your task, do it and delete the TODO.
Otherwise, add a URL, an issue number such as `#412`, or a ticket such as `FOO-412` to the same comment.
Do not invent one: if no issue exists, ask whether to file one.
Level: module
